+ * @basis: exact held child socket basis after successful reconstruction
+ * @inherited: exact GMainContext the basis was reconstructed against
+ * @replacement: fresh GMainContext the rebuilt monitor I/O thread runs
+ *
+ * A hot-fork child rebuilds its monitor I/O thread's GMainContext, because
+ * GLib will not let a new thread acquire the inherited one.  While input is
+ * held no source is attached, so the held socket follows by recording the
+ * replacement as the chardev's and the basis's context; the sources that
+ * release attaches then land in it.
